🎯 Key Takeaways
Python source code is compiled into bytecode in CPython.
The Python Virtual Machine executes bytecode.
.pyc files contain cached bytecode.
__pycache__ commonly stores cached bytecode.
Namespaces map names to objects.
LEGB defines the basic name lookup order.
Python variables are names referring to objects.
id() provides an object's identity.
== compares values.
is compares object identity.
Mutable objects can be modified.
Immutable objects cannot be modified in place.
CPython uses reference counting as a major part of memory management.
Python also has garbage collection for certain unreachable cycles.
sys.path shows module search locations.
sys.modules contains modules already loaded by the import system.
